  <div id="lessonContent">
    <h2>1. What is a div in HTML?</h2>
    <p><b>div</b> means <b>Division</b>. It is a box used to <b>group big content together</b>. For example - a full section, a header, a card, a footer.</p>
    <p>Think like this: A website is made of many boxes. Every box is a <b>div</b>. Inside a div, you can put heading, paragraph, image, button, form — anything.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>Example:</b> Header is one div. Main content is one div. Footer is one div. A product card is one div.</div>
    <h2>2. Basic div Example</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;div&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;h2&gt;</span><span class="text">My Name is Ali</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h2&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;p&gt;</span><span class="text">I am learning HTML.</span><span class="tag">&lt;/p&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/div&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b><div class="demo-div"><h3 style="margin:0 0 5px">My Name is Ali</h3><p style="margin:0">I am learning HTML.</p></div></div>
    <div class="note"><b>Important:</b> div by itself has no design. It only groups content. Design is added later with CSS in Lesson 11.</div>
    <h2>3. What is a span in HTML?</h2>
    <p><b>span</b> is used to <b>style a small part of text</b> inside a line. For example - make one word red, bold, or different color.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;p&gt;</span><span class="text">My name is </span><span class="tag">&lt;span&gt;</span><span class="text">Ali</span><span class="tag">&lt;/span&gt;</span><span class="text"> and I love coding.</span><span class="tag">&lt;/p&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b><p style="margin:0">My name is <span class="demo-span">Ali</span> and I love coding.</p></div>
    <h2>4. div vs span - The Biggest Difference</h2>
    <p>This is the most asked question in interviews. Learn this table by heart:</p>
    <table>
      <tr><th>div</th><th>span</th></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Block Element</b> - Takes full width, starts on a new line</td><td><b>Inline Element</b> - Takes only as much width as needed, stays in same line</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Used for <b>big sections</b> - header, card, footer</td><td>Used for <b>small text</b> - one word, one line part</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Example: A full box</td><td>Example: One word in a paragraph</td></tr>
    </table>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">&lt;!-- div = New Line --&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;div&gt;</span><span class="text">Hello</span><span class="tag">&lt;/div&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;div&gt;</span><span class="text">World</span><span class="tag">&lt;/div&gt;</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">&lt;!-- span = Same Line --&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;p&gt;</span><span class="text">Hello </span><span class="tag">&lt;span&gt;</span><span class="text">World</span><span class="tag">&lt;/span&gt;</span><span class="tag">&lt;/p&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b><div style="background:#e0f2fe;padding:8px;margin:4px 0;border-radius:6px">Hello</div><div style="background:#e0f2fe;padding:8px;margin:4px 0;border-radius:6px">World</div><p style="margin:8px 0 0">Hello <span class="demo-span">World</span> (span stays in same line)</p></div>
    <h2>5. class and id - Name for div</h2>
    <p>When you have many divs, you need to give them a name so CSS can find them. We use <b>class</b> and <b>id</b> for that.</p>
    <table>
      <tr><th>class</th><th>id</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Can be used for <b>many</b> divs (same name)</td><td>Used for <b>only one</b> div (unique name)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Example: All product cards = class="card"</td><td>Example: Header = id="header"</td></tr>
      <tr><td>In CSS: .card { }</td><td>In CSS: #header { }</td></tr>
    </table>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="attr">class</span>=<span class="val">"card"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text"> Product 1 </span><span class="tag">&lt;/div&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="attr">class</span>=<span class="val">"card"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text"> Product 2 </span><span class="tag">&lt;/div&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"header"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text"> My Website Header </span><span class="tag">&lt;/div&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="note"><b>Rule:</b> class = For many elements. id = For only one element. You will use class 90% of the time in real projects.</div>
    <h2>6. Full Example - Website Structure with div</h2>
    <p>Every website is made like this:</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"header"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;h1&gt;</span><span class="text">My Website</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h1&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/div&gt;</span><br><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="attr">class</span>=<span class="val">"main"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;h2&gt;</span><span class="text">Welcome</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h2&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;p&gt;</span><span class="text">This is my first website.</span><span class="tag">&lt;/p&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/div&gt;</span><br><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="attr">class</span>=<span class="val">"card"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;h3&gt;</span><span class="text">Product 1</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h3&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;p&gt;</span><span class="text">Price: 1500</span><span class="tag">&lt;/p&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/div&gt;</span><br><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"footer"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;p&gt;</span><span class="text">© 2026 My Website</span><span class="tag">&lt;/p&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/div&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result - Website Layout:</b><div style="background:#0f172a;color:white;padding:10px;border-radius:8px;text-align:center;margin-bottom:6px"><b>My Website</b></div><div style="background:#f8fafc;padding:10px;border-radius:8px;margin-bottom:6px"><b>Welcome</b><br>This is my first website.</div><div style="background:#e0f2fe;padding:10px;border-radius:8px;margin-bottom:6px"><b>Product 1</b><br>Price: 1500</div><div style="background:#e2e8f0;padding:10px;border-radius:8px;text-align:center">© 2026 My Website</div></div>
    <h2>7. Homework - Practice for 2 Minutes</h2>
    <p>Create a page with:</p>
    <p>1. One <b>div id="header"</b> with your name<br>2. One <b>div class="card"</b> with your favourite food<br>3. One paragraph where one word is inside a <b>span</b></p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> div = Big box, Block, New Line | span = Small text, Inline, Same Line | class = For many, .card in CSS | id = For one, #header in CSS | div + class + id = Foundation of every website layout</div>
    <p><b>Next Step:</b> After this lesson, go to <a href="/lesson9">Lesson 9 - Semantic HTML</a> to learn header, nav, main, section, footer.</p>
    <a id="playgroundLink" class="btn" href="/playground">▶ Try it Yourself - Playground</a><br><br>
